[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139526,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Glomus tumour is a mesenchymal neoplasm showing differentiation analogous to perivascular cells of the glomus body.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139527,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8711/0 Glomus tumour, NOS</p>\r\n<p>8711/1 Glomus tumour of uncertain malignant potential</p>\r\n<p>8711/3 Glomus tumour, malignant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139528,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F36.Y &amp; XH47J2 Other specified benign neoplasm of eye or ocular adnexa &amp; Glomus tumour, NOS</p>\r\n<p>2D0Y &amp; XH21E6 Other specified malignant neoplasms of eye or ocular adnexa &amp; Glomus tumour, malignant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139529,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139530,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Glomangioma; symplastic glomus tumour; malignant glomus tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139531,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours may arise in the soft tissue or bone {17036559;3019113;32604167}. The orbit and eyelid are rarely involved {32962404;14270138}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139532,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pain is a common manifestation {17027805}. Eye tumours may present with blindness and/or proptosis {18447675;23216695}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139533,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Glomus tumours rarely involve the eye; they have been reported in children and adults, with no clear sex predilection {14270138;18447675;22642677}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139534,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most tumours are sporadic. A minority result from a germline <em>GLMN</em> {11845407} or <em>NF1</em> mutation {19991403;19738042}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139535,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sporadic non-ophthalmic tumours frequently harbour gene fusions involving <em>NOTCH1</em>, <em>NOTCH2</em>, or <em>NOTCH3</em>, with multiple potential partners (e.g. <em>MIR143</em>, <em>CARMN</em>) {23999936;32604167;34245196}; fusions are less common in malignant tumours {32604167}. A minority have mutations of <em>BRAF</em> {22317887;28834810} or <em>KRAS</em> {22317887}. The molecular pathogenesis appears to vary based on anatomical location. These molecular features are based on non-ophthalmic tumours; however, there is no reason to suspect a difference from those arising elsewhere in the body.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139536,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are typically small and circumscribed. They may appear purple-blue, and solid or cystic {21371130}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139537,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Morphologically tumours are composed of sheets of round to polygonal cells. The cytoplasm is eosinophilic to amphophilic with well-defined membranes. The nuclei are centrally located, round to ovoid, and monomorphic; mitotic activity is inconspicuous. Tumours have a delicate capillary-sized vasculature. The intervening stroma may be myxoid to collagenous; glomangioma is additionally characterized by ectatic and branching vascular spaces. Symplastic tumours contain marked nuclear pleomorphism, but no mitotic activity. Malignant tumours are classified based on: (1)&nbsp;atypical mitotic figures, (2)&nbsp;nuclear pleomorphism and high mitotic activity, or (3)&nbsp;size &gt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;mm and deep anatomical location {11145243}.</p>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry is typically positive for SMA and h-caldesmon, with variable staining for desmin and CD34.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139538,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139539,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>NOTCH family rearrangement or <em>BRAF</em> or <em>KRAS</em> mutation, in the appropriate clinical and histomorphological context, may be diagnostically helpful.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139540,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential</em>: sheets of round-polygonal cells with well-defined cell borders, and monomorphic round central nuclei.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable</em>: immunoreactivity for SMA or h-caldesmon; NOTCH family rearrangement or mutations involving <em>BRAF</em> or <em>KRAS</em> in malignant tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139541,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139542,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 271,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Conventional glomus tumours are benign. Malignant tumours are locally aggressive with the potential for metastasis {11145243;33133513}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]